  "steps": [
    "Masalas - Salt, 1/2 tsp red chilli powder, 1/2 tsp garam masala, 1 tsp aamchur, 1/4 tsp pepper, 1/2 tsp jeer powder, 1/2 tsp coriander powder.",
    "Boil Soya Chunks & Wash with cold water. Squeeze out the excess liquid and keep aside.",
    "In a pan, add a little oil and then add green chilli & garlic paste. Sauté and then add onions.",
    "Let the onions cook and then add carrots and corn. Let it cook on low flame for 4-5 mins & then add the masalas, rice flour, soya chunks & mint. Mix well and cook for 3-4 mins. Turn off the flame and let the mixture cool down.",
    "Before you grind, add in the slice of wholewheat bread. Grind the mixture and then roll into tikkis.",
    "Brush oil on a non-stick pan and let the tikkis cook on low flame on both sides until golden brown. This will take around 10-12 minutes.",
    "Before you dig in, let the kebabs cool down a little so that it holds onto its texture.",
    "Serve it with some greek yogurt dip (Yogurt + Pinch of Black Salt & Chilli powder + Pinch of sugar + pomegranate)"
  ],
